#Problem APEX 1.4.18

DOCUMENT();

# Load whatever macros you need for the problem
loadMacros(
  "PGstandard.pl",
  "PGML.pl",
  "PGchoicemacros.pl",
  "PGcourse.pl"
);

## Updated July 2023

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 1;

$a = random(2,6,1);
$b = random(2,8,2);
$c = random(-10,10,1);
$d = $a*$c;

TEXT(beginproblem());

BEGIN_PGML
Evaluate the limits.

[```
   g(x) = \begin{cases}
	[$a] x + [$b]  & x < [$c] \\
	[$d] & x = [$c] \\
	[$a] x - [$b]  & x > [$c]
	\end{cases}
```]

Enter *DNE* if the limit does not exist.

a) [`` \lim_{x \to [$c]^-} g(x) = ``] [_]{$a*$c + $b}{10}

b) [`` \lim_{x \to [$c]^+} g(x) = ``]  [_]{$a*$c - $b}{10}

c) [`` \lim_{x \to [$c]} g(x) = ``] [_]{"DNE"}{10}

d) [`` g([$c]) = ``] [_]{$d}{10}
END_PGML

#####################################################################

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Since the left- and right-hand limits at [` x = [$c] `] are different, [`` \lim_{x \to [$c]} g(x) ``] does not exist. Evaluate [` g(x) `] at [` x = [$c] `] using the definition.
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();    



